river|Flowing watercourse rather than lake is intended; destination wording avoids claiming every river reaches the sea. Footpath and old mill translate faithfully, and legacy overlap stays evidence only.
to|Destination preposition is supported by Oxford ordinal zero. Infinitive marker source ordinal one is not drafted because ledger POS does not support its category; the gap remains visible in boundary audit.
willing|Chosen readiness is distinct from ability or successful completion. Help-to construction and natural standalone Vietnamese sẵn lòng checked, with no restriction to a particular tense.
accomplishment|Effortful achievement rather than any completed activity is the boundary. Trail completion and volunteer attribution align in Vietnamese; major is example intensity, not a required property.
fortunate|Luck and favourable opportunity are not equated with wealth. Finding accommodation before rain translates faithfully and does not imply the finding caused the favourable weather.
